{#-
  Services (spec S6, roadmap Phase 6).

  Register: identical to Home. The spec is explicit that the cinematic tone
  runs across commercial pages too (S1) -- no shift into corporate-brochure
  voice, no "solutions" language, no invented client logos or testimonials.

  Every claim here describes a capability the team offers, not work already
  delivered. There is no shipped commercial work yet (S2), so there are no
  case studies, no client names, and no metrics. Those get added once real
  engagements exist -- see the placeholder list.
-#}

<div class="wrapper">
  <header class="region" style="--region-space-top: var(--space-xl-2xl); --region-space-bottom: var(--space-m)">
    <div class="flow">
      <h1 class="font-display">Services</h1>
      <p class="hero-subline" style="margin-inline: 0">
        Engineering capability, available on contract. The same people, tools, and discipline behind the
        competition work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="automation-heading" style="--region-space-bottom: var(--space-m)">
    <div class="service-line flow">
      <p class="service-line__index">01</p>
      <h2 id="automation-heading" class="font-display text-step-2">Industrial Automation</h2>
      <p>
        Boutique automation work, industry-agnostic. Process control, instrumentation, and the integration
        layer between machines that were never designed to talk to each other.
      </p>
      <ul class="service-tags | cluster gutter-xs-s" role="list">
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Process control</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Instrumentation</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Systems integration</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Retrofit</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="robotics-heading" style="--region-space-bottom: var(--space-m)">
    <div class="service-line flow">
      <p class="service-line__index">02</p>
      <h2 id="robotics-heading" class="font-display text-step-2">Industrial Robotics</h2>
      <p>
        Industry- and form-factor-agnostic. Manipulators, mobile platforms, and purpose-built mechanisms —
        designed, built, and instrumented for the environment they actually have to survive.
      </p>
      <ul class="service-tags | cluster gutter-xs-s" role="list">
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Mechanical design</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Controls</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Perception</li>
        <li class="button" data-small-button>Prototyping</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="cyber-heading" style="--region-space-bottom: var(--space-m)">
    <div class="service-line flow">
      <p class="service-line__index">03</p>
      <h2 id="cyber-heading" class="font-display text-step-2">Cybersecurity</h2>
      <p>
        Offensive-minded security work across the full surface — not just the parts that live on a network.
      </p>

      <div class="grid" data-layout="thirds" style="--flow-space: var(--space-m)">
        <div class="pillar flow">
          <h3 class="font-display">Offensive Security</h3>
          <p>Penetration testing and adversarial assessment against systems as deployed, not as documented.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar flow">
          <h3 class="font-display">Physical Security</h3>
          <p>Access control, perimeter, and the seams where physical and digital controls stop covering for each other.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar flow">
          <h3 class="font-display">CEMA</h3>
          <p>Cyberspace electromagnetic activities — the spectrum treated as terrain rather than background noise.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar flow">
          <h3 class="font-display">CPS Security</h3>
          <p>Cyber-physical systems, where a software failure becomes a mechanical one and the blast radius is measured in metres.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="client-heading">
    <div class="sponsor-cta flow">
      <h2 id="client-heading" class="font-display">Start a Conversation</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us what you're building, breaking, or defending. If it's outside what we can do well, we'll say so
        rather than take the contract.
      </p>

      {#- Separate form id and subject from the Home sponsor CTA (roadmap
         Phase 6: "Client inquiry CTA, separate from the sponsor form"), so
         client mail is sortable from sponsor mail in the same inbox. #}
      {% set formId = "client" %}
      {% set formSubject = "Ghurab — new client inquiry" %}
      {% set reasonLabel = "Service line" %}
      {% set reasonOptions = ["Industrial Automation", "Industrial Robotics", "Cybersecurity", "Not sure yet"] %}
      {% set submitLabel = "Send Inquiry" %}
      {% set showMessage = true %}
      {% include "partials/inquiry-form.njk" %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

